# =========================
# STC — secrets & user data
# =========================
# Never commit real user data / secrets. Templates (the *.example.* files)
# ARE committed so the repo is usable; the real files they spawn are ignored.
#
# user/ is DENY-BY-DEFAULT, templates are allowed back in by exception.
#
# It used to list the personal files by name, and that silently failed open:
# anything new in user/ was tracked unless someone remembered to add it. On
# 2026-09-02 two personal drafts (a grant application and a LinkedIn profile
# rewrite) sat unignored in a repo that has a GitHub remote and publishes its
# core/ half — one sweeping `git add` away from being public. The same class of
# leak was already fixed once by hand ("убрать имя пользователя из общей
# справки по кириллице"), which is the signal that naming files one by one is
# the wrong shape for this rule.
stc.yaml
user/*
!user/*.example.md
!user/secrets.env.example
!user/projects/
user/projects/*
!user/projects/example.example.md

# =========================
# Deploy output
# =========================
# Rendered config is generated; source of truth is STC repo
graphify-out/
deploy/_rendered/
*.rendered.json
*.rendered.md
deploy/_manifest.json

# Doc-backend state (incremental hashes per harness)
deploy/doc_backend/.state/
*.infra-content-state*.json

# =========================
# Python
# =========================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# =========================
# OS / editor
# =========================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# =========================
# Logs
# =========================
*.log
tmp/

# =========================
# Corpus / scratch (PRIVATE — real transcripts)
# =========================
# scratchpad/ holds throwaway experiments over REAL conversation transcripts.
# The corpus itself now lives OUTSIDE the repo ($STC_CORPUS, default
# ~/.stc/.corpus/corpus.jsonl) — this entry is the second lock so a stray
# `git add -A` can never publish personal data to a public remote.
scratchpad/
*.corpus.jsonl
corpus.jsonl

# =========================
# Site / deploy tooling caches
# =========================
# Cloudflare Wrangler caches hold account credentials — never commit.
site/.wrangler/
